# Kotlin SDUI engine

- Keep the engine in `sdui/` (`model`, `registry`, `runtime`, `render`). Screens in `ui/`. Leaf chrome in `ui/components/` is shared by the SDUI and static twins.
- Parse with `kotlinx.serialization`. Prefer a sealed `SduiNode` / `SduiAction` over `Map<String, Any>`.
- Registry maps `type` → `@Composable (node, dispatcher) -> Unit`. No giant `when` in `MainActivity`.
- Recurse through children. Collections use `LazyRow` / `LazyColumn` with stable keys.
- Actions go through `ActionDispatcher`. Bindings resolve against `SduiState`, not ViewModel fields named after home-page widgets.
- Images load with Coil. Do not block the main thread on JSON parse; measure parse vs compose separately for `PERF.md`.

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD — page-specific type + hardcoded tap
@Composable fun CarRail(cars: List<Car>) { /* onClick = { nav.detail() } */ }

// ✅ GOOD
registry.register("card") { node, dispatcher ->
    Card(onClick = { dispatcher.dispatch(node.actions) }) { SduiChildren(node, dispatcher) }
}
```
